    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;4.01</strong> The Spigelman classification of duodenal polyposis in familial adenomatous polyposis {2571019}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Lancet. 2(8666) Spigelman AD, Williams CB, Talbot IC, Domizio P, Phillips RK. Upper gastrointestinal cancer in patients with familial adenomatous polyposis. 783-5. Copyright 1989, with permission from Elsevier. ",
    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"155\">\r\n<p><strong>Polyp feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td colspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"363\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>Allocated points</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>1</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>2</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>3</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"155\">\r\n<p><strong>Number</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">1&ndash;4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">5&ndash;20</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">&gt;&nbsp;20</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"155\">\r\n<p><strong>Size (mm)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">1&ndash;4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">5&ndash;10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">&gt;&nbsp;10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"155\">\r\n<p><strong>Histology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">Tubular</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">Tubulovillous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">Villous</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"155\">\r\n<p><strong>Degree of dysplasia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">Low (mild)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">Low (moderate)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"121\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">High (severe)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan=\"4\" valign=\"top\" width=\"518\">\r\n<p><strong>Correlation of points with stages:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Stage 0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 0 points</p>\r\n<p>Stage I&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1&ndash;4 points</p>\r\n<p>Stage II&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 5&ndash;6 points</p>\r\n<p>Stage III&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 7&ndash;8 points</p>\r\n<p>Stage IV&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 9&ndash;12 points</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Note: Stages&nbsp;III and&nbsp;IV represent severe polyposis. Originally designed as a three-tiered dysplastic system (mild to severe), this table has been updated to include the preferred current two-tiered system {29998424; 14752072}.</p>",
